NUM-44: compare month/day dates with the current date in the same 365-day calendar

SWEEP_START, SWEEP_END and a DAYOFYEAR rule value given as MM/DD are stored
as the day of year they have in the non-leap year 1947 (03/01 = 60,
12/31 = 365), but were compared with the day of year of the current date,
which in a leap year is one higher from Mar 1 on (03/01 = 61,
12/31 = 366). Every date after Feb 28 was therefore matched one day early in
leap years and Dec 31 was never matched. Add datetime_dayOfYear365(), which
gives the current date's day in the same 365-day calendar (Feb 29 = 59.5,
between Feb 28 and Mar 1), and use it for the DAYOFYEAR premise and the
sweeping season. Non-leap years are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-44_swmm530.patch

